// The roof pattern (D241, D258, D290): roof cubes, cut to slopes and corners, drawn as a
// roof from their neighbours (`layout::roofs`, `roofing`): the covering their sloped surface
// in its material, so thick and pushed out by its height, its rows on level lines; each
// line its neighbours make (ridge, hip, valley, eave, verge, flashing) and its frame
// (rafters, battens) a module of pieces. Kinds numbered from 2048. A material of it
// (shakes, slate, thatch) is a few lines naming this pattern and its pack, which gives its
// covering and, where its outline is its look, its own pieces; with none, it is laid on this
// pattern's frame and capped by its board ridge, so a new covering needs nothing more.
//
// eaves       how far its covering is carried on past its cubes' open edges, drawn only
// roof        rows: courses one copy of the covering's texture holds up the slope; phase:
//             where a course's lower edge falls on it; thick: the covering's thickness;
//             relief: how far its texture's height pushes each course out; tint; rafter and
//             batten sizes; parts: the module of pieces each line and the frame is, in its
//             material, with its ends' material and tint (a pack with its own ridge draws it
//             in its Piece atlas)
// textures    the texture sets every roof shares: its shared pieces' atlas (Trim), rafters'
//             bark (Log) and ends, battens' and the ridge's boards, flashing's mortar; a pack
//             adds its Covering, and may give its rafters' own Log and its own pieces' atlas
//             (Piece)
// details     the fine grain laid over its textures near (D362): wood's on its boards; a
//             pack adds its covering's, stone's or wood's, and its rafters'
// dress       its shared pieces (art/kits/roof): the board along a verge, an eave's fascia,
//             the flashing, the valley's lining, each to its contract (size, anchor), seated
//             on the deck or the covering by the layout, so one fits every covering; the
//             frame's pine rafters and sawn battens; and a ridge of two lapped boards
// meets       a roof is drawn over what it rests on, which it neither caps nor ends against
// toughness  how much damage a cube takes before it is destroyed (D193): a roof is light
// damage      how its covering breaks as it loses its health (D305): a shingle, slate or
//             shake at a time, the gaps between them the lowest share of its height map
// burns       what it does in a fire (D377, terra_build::fire): None for slate; a covering
//             of wood or straw says its own in its pack
// look        what the material bench holds every covering of it to (`cargo xtask look`, D386,
//             terra_build::look): its covering's texels a metre, its sharpness from 1, 2 and
//             5 m, its brightness against an 18% grey card lit and in shade, its values'
//             spread, and the most of each texture set drawn stretched, its own pieces'
//             atlas, measured against itself, its own
(
    pattern: Roof,
    toughness: (health: 200, breaks: Bits),
    burns: None,
    damage: {
        Covering: Shingles(share: 0.22),
    },
    eaves: 0.5,
    roof: (
        thick: 0.03,
        relief: 0.03,
        rafter: 0.14,
        batten: (0.06, 0.025),
        parts: {
            Ridge: (module: "ridge", material: Board, tint: (0.66, 0.62, 0.58)),
            Hip: (module: "ridge", material: Board, tint: (0.66, 0.62, 0.58)),
            Valley: (module: "valley", material: Trim),
            Eave: (module: "eave", material: Trim, tint: (0.58, 0.54, 0.5)),
            Verge: (module: "verge", material: Trim, tint: (0.58, 0.54, 0.5)),
            // Where the covering meets something standing on or beside the roof (D343): an
            // apron where the roof rises to it, steps up a sloping line, a back gutter where it
            // falls to it; the one board for each until a piece is made for each.
            Flashing: (module: "flashing", material: Trim, tint: (0.62, 0.6, 0.58)),
            Step: (module: "flashing", material: Trim, tint: (0.62, 0.6, 0.58)),
            Gutter: (module: "flashing", material: Trim, tint: (0.62, 0.6, 0.58)),
            Rafter: (module: "rafter", material: Log, ends: Some(LogEnd)),
            Batten: (module: "batten", material: Board, tint: (0.9, 0.9, 0.9)),
        },
    ),
    textures: {
        Trim: (path: "materials/roof_pieces", metres: (1.0, 1.0)),
        Log: (path: "materials/pine_bark", metres: (1.0, 1.0)),
        LogEnd: (path: "materials/log_end", metres: (1.0, 1.0)),
        Board: (path: "materials/weathered_planks", metres: (2.0, 2.0)),
        Flashing: (path: "materials/white_stucco", metres: (1.0, 1.0)),
    },
    details: {
        Board: (path: "materials/detail_wood", metres: 0.4, strength: 0.8),
    },
    dress: (
        pieces: Some("data/kits/pieces/roof.ron"),
    ),
    meets: Some((weight: 0, end: None, carries: None)),
    // The bench's targets (D386), set from shakes' and slate's numbers on 2026-10-16 (texel
    // density 640 and 853; sharpness 19.9, 19.8, 29.0% and 21.4, 26.9, 21.8%; values 5 to
    // 120 and 11 to 70; 0.27 to 0.32 and 0.17 to 0.18 of the card lit, 0.43 and 0.35 on the
    // slope away from the sun), a little under the worse of them; the own pieces' atlas
    // (Piece), measured against itself, and the shared trims their own.
    look: (
        surface: Covering,
        density: 600.0,
        sharpness: (17.0, 17.0, 19.0),
        lit: (0.18, 0.4),
        shade: (0.21, 0.4),
        sky: (0.45, 0.9),
        values: (45.0, 140.0),
        stretch: (
            smeared: 2.0,
            streaked: 0.5,
            roles: {Covering: (18.0, 1.5), Piece: (45.0, 3.5), Trim: (3.5, 1.5)},
        ),
    ),
)
